   "item": {
    "subject_key": "ap-precalculus",
    "unit_number": 1,
    "topic_code": "1.14",
    "topic_title": "Function Model Construction and Application",
    "stem": "A bicycle rental shop charges a fixed booking fee plus a constant hourly rate. A 2-hour rental costs 34 dollars, and a 5-hour rental costs 58 dollars. Let C(h) be the total cost, in dollars, for a rental lasting h hours. What total cost does this model predict for a 7-hour rental?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "56 dollars",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Omitted fixed fee: Multiplying the hourly rate by 7 gives 8(7) = 56 dollars, but this includes only the hourly charges. The total must also include the 18-dollar booking fee. Fix: Subtract the hourly charges from a known total to find the booking fee."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "90 dollars",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Misidentified intercept: Using C(h) = 34+8h treats the 2-hour rental total as the booking fee. The 34 dollars already includes 16 dollars in hourly charges, so this model counts those charges twice. Fix: Find C(0) by subtracting two hours of charges from the 2-hour total."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "74 dollars",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "The hourly rate is (58−34)/(5−2) = 8 dollars per hour, and the booking fee is 34−8(2) = 18 dollars. Thus C(h) = 18+8h, so C(7) = 74 dollars."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "119 dollars",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Proportional-model error: Computing (34/2)(7) assumes the total cost is proportional to rental duration. That ignores the booking fee and predicts 85 dollars for 5 hours, contradicting the given 58 dollars. Fix: Compute the hourly rate from changes in cost and time, not total cost divided by time."
     }
    ]
   },
